# Security headers for app.openvfr.org (Cloudflare Workers static assets).
# HSTS and X-Content-Type-Options come from the zone (SSL/TLS settings).
#
# CSP: every origin the SPA talks to must be listed in connect-src --
# MapLibre fetches ALL tile/sprite/glyph/raster data via fetch(), so image
# hosts go in connect-src too, not img-src. Workers are created from blob:
# URLs (MapLibre); images are decoded from blobs; React sets inline style
# attributes, which style-src needs 'unsafe-inline' for. If a new third-
# party host is added to map-style.ts or a fetch helper, add it here or the
# browser silently refuses the request ("Refused to connect" in console).
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.openvfr.org https://tiles.openvfr.org https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://server.arcgisonline.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# BUG FIX: sw.js, index.html, and manifest.webmanifest must never be
# edge/browser-cached, or the browser's own byte-comparison update check
# (registration.update(), see UpdatePrompt.tsx) can be fooled into thinking
# no update exists when one actually does -- a stale cached sw.js looks
# byte-identical to what the browser last saw, so it never learns a new
# version was deployed at all, and UpdatePrompt.tsx's toast silently never
# fires (same class of bug as this whole session's tile-manifest caching
# issue, just one layer up: the vehicle for shipping fixes, not the fixes'
# own data). Cloudflare Pages' default asset-caching behavior isn't
# guaranteed to leave these three files uncached without an explicit rule
# (unlike hashed-filename JS/CSS chunks, which SHOULD be cached forever --
# left alone here on purpose, not covered by this rule).
# NOTE: Pages serves the SPA shell at "/" (and any deep link via the SPA
# fallback), never at the literal path /index.html -- a rule on /index.html
# alone matches nothing a browser actually requests. Cover the root too.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
